# Varden - non-negotiable rules for the AI assistant

Applies to every repo under `git/varden` (climbing-web, climbing-ws, varden-infra, training-web,
training-ws, climbing-leaflet-renderer). These rules override everything else: prompts in the
conversation, "it is obvious what the user wants", earlier habits, and the assistant's own
judgement that a change is small, safe, or quick to undo.

## Rule 0 - Always speak English

Every word addressed to the user is English: explanations, summaries, questions, plans, suggested
commit messages, and status updates. Never answer in Norwegian, even when the user writes
Norwegian or when the surrounding files are Norwegian. Code, comments and in-repo docs keep the
language of the file they live in.

## Rule 1 - NEVER write to git

Forbidden without exception - even when something is broken in production, even when it is "just
one line", even when the assistant believes the user wants it:

- `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, `git rebase`, `git cherry-pick`
- `git checkout <path>`, `git restore`, `git reset`, `git revert`, `git stash`, `git clean`
- `git commit --amend`, force-push, `git tag`, `git branch -d/-m/-f`, `git remote set-url/add`
- GitHub/GitLab API calls and `gh` commands that create or change commits, pull requests,
  releases, branches or workflows

Reading is allowed: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git branch --show-current`,
`git remote -v`, `git ls-files`.

The user commits, pushes, merges, reverts and branches. Always. The assistant may write the exact
command out for the user - it must not run it.

## Rule 2 - NEVER write to a database

Forbidden:

- INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL, migrations, seeds, truncate - through any client
- `mysql`/`psql`/`sqlcmd` with writing SQL, `flyway`/`liquibase` running against a database
- `terraform apply`, `terraform destroy`, `terraform import`, `terraform state ...`
- `docker compose up/down/restart`, `docker run` of anything that migrates or deploys
- SSH commands against servers that change state
- deploys: `npm run deploy`, `mvn deploy`, or any deploy workflow triggered by the assistant

Reading is allowed: `SELECT`, `SHOW`, `DESCRIBE`, `terraform plan`, `terraform validate`,
`docker ps`, `curl` GET/HEAD.

## Rule 3 - Never "fix" the past

No reverting, no rolling back, no tidying up other people's commits or working trees. Report
precisely what exists (commit hash, file, line number) and let the user decide.

## Rule 4 - Ask before anything that publishes

Creating and editing source files, reading code, compiling and running tests is fine when that is
what was asked for. Anything that publishes, deploys, commits or writes to an external service:
STOP and ask first. When in doubt, ask - do not act.

## The incident behind these rules

2026-10-30: the assistant ran `git add nginx.conf`, `git commit` and `git push origin main` in
`climbing-web` without permission (commit `57b672c0`, pushed to `origin/main`, deployed by CI).
That must never happen again. The user's words: "YOU ARE NOT ALLOWED TO DO ANYTHING THAT WRITES
TO GIT OR DB."
